  "body": "## What\n\n`MCPX_TEST_REQUIRE` had two parsers in the same package, and CI's `python3` entry was enforced by nothing. Both are fixed here.\n\n- **One parser.** `parseRequireList` in `pkgs/mcpx/internal/testsupport/require.go` is now the only place the variable is parsed. It states the label and wildcard rules once (`realsoftware`/`real`/`*` demand every real server; `*` never names a binary), lower-cases every entry, and `realRequired` in `realserver.go` calls it instead of keeping its own copy. Case is insignificant for runtime binaries and real servers alike — `MCPX_TEST_REQUIRE=RealSoftware` previously demanded a *binary* named `realsoftware` (failing a missing runtime) while demanding no real server at all.\n- **Suite-level enforcement.** `MissingRequiredBinaries()` checks every listed entry against `PATH`, and `TestRequiredBinariesAreOnPath` fails the suite when one is absent. Before this, enforcement was purely per-test, so an entry no test passes to `RequireBinary` — `python3` in `.github/workflows/mcpx.yml:178` — was checked by nothing and a missing `python3` narrowed the run silently. `python3` stays in the workflow list, now with a consumer.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `go test ./internal/testsupport/ -count=1` — pass (unset and with `MCPX_TEST_REQUIRE=deno,bun,node,python3`)\n- `MCPX_TEST_REQUIRE=deno,mcpx-no-such-binary-5584 go test ./internal/testsupport/ -run TestRequiredBinariesAreOnPath` — fails naming the absent binary, as intended\n- New tests pin the case rules (`RealSoftware`/`REALSOFTWARE`/`realsoftware`), that labels and `*` never leak into the binary set, and the suite-level check itself.\n\nCloses #6904\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796736142&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7696&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7696&signature=247b3510497cad65d47bd2cdea034f0c11aac26cb25269d70d8496fdf5208438\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7696?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
